<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teatro Regio (Parma)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1829">1829</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Teatro Regio di Parma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Teatro Regio is an opera house in Parma built for Duchess Marie Louise by the architect Nicola Bettoli and opened in 1829 with an opera by Vincenzo Bellini. Known for its demanding audiences, it is closely associated with the music of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi">Giuseppe Verdi</a> and hosts the annual Verdi Festival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teatro-regio-parma.jpg" alt="Teatro Regio (Parma)" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stefano Sansavini · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2018_parma_035.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the nineteenth century Marie Louise sponsored public works, including the <b>Teatro Regio</b>, opened in 1829, and a bridge over the Taro.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
